      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Bagtown museum showcases a Model T, firetrucks, and a 1928 Baldwin steam engine, letting visitors step back into early transportation history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.garrettheritage.com/history-culture",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Historic National Road runs through Bagtown, a 19th‑century artery that opened the western frontier for pioneers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.garrettheritage.com/history-culture",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Casselman River Bridge in Bagtown, listed on the National Register of Historic Places, was once considered a technological marvel of its era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.garrettheritage.com/history-culture",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
